{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149969-entitlements-for-the-directional-courts","id":149969,"title":"Entitlements for the Directional Courts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-26T20:15:42-07:00","id":149969,"title":"Entitlements for the Directional Courts?","content":"I may be running a game set in Hong Kong and as such need more info on the Directional Courts. Do they have any specific Entitlements or those that might be repurposed with minimal work? I fully intend to bring in the Phantom Tong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T14:21:10-07:00","id":150789,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that, aside from a token mention in Lords of Summer, everything there is to know about the Directions can be found in Winter Masques.<br /> <br /> I've run few games using them, though, and so I have some notes that might be of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-01-2014, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:29:33-07:00","id":153354,"title":"","content":"College of Worms. Not sure of what the divining traditions of the East are but I'm sure they are there.<br /> <br /> Magistrates of the Wax Mask. Requires a little more changing. Probably change the mien appearance and the token to something more symbolically tied to eastern traditions. However, the importance of celebrations (and tea ceremonies) give the magistrates a good stepping stone to start off on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","user":"TrickyBoots","date":". 05-30-2014, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T22:39:03-07:00","id":153555,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, the North Court would probably either maintain a branch of the Duchy of the Icebound Heart or something similar. Love is a weakness for the Fae to exploit; best to guard yourself with heartbreak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T12:44:21-07:00","id":155845,"title":"","content":"I'm sure the Goldspinners show up in the East Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T13:38:08-07:00","id":155880,"title":"","content":"There's a couple in my index that I think work for all Courts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149969-entitlements-for-the-directional-courts?p=153555#post153555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, the North Court would probably either maintain a branch of the Duchy of the Icebound Heart or something similar. Love is a weakness for the Fae to exploit; best to guard yourself with heartbreak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubt it.<br /> <br /> Winter is all about &quot;I'll never be hurt again&quot;. The Duchy is all about not letting themselves feel anything genuine encase they end up hurt.<br /> <br /> North is all about &quot;I'll embrace being hurt, so you can't threaten me with pain&quot;. So they wouldn't guard their hearts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T14:07:29-07:00","id":155934,"title":"","content":"The writeup for North has a Court-mandated ban on love and physical relationships. Some mercenary-minded Dukes might make a fair profit by punishing North Courtiers who flaunt this rule with heartbreak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T14:11:40-07:00","id":155940,"title":"","content":"But those mercenaries would probably be Winter or East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:13:49-07:00","id":157024,"title":"","content":"Pilgrims of the Endless Road. Their focus on self improvement through honing their bodies and minds really dovetails nicely with stereotypically Asian motifs of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue. You don't have to do much reskinning to these guys, as the culinary tradition of Asia has an adventurous and complex reputation. Also, the idea of the magical properties of foods are pretty common in the region's folklore.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:20:31-07:00","id":157032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149969-entitlements-for-the-directional-courts#post149969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be running a game set in Hong Kong and as such need more info on the Directional Courts. Do they have any specific Entitlements or those that might be repurposed with minimal work? I fully intend to bring in the Phantom Tong.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's set in Hong Kong you're likely to see a blending of the Directional and Seasonal courts (Hong Kong is very mixed-culture).<br /> <br /> The Directional courts, if you're basing them on the idea of feng shui, would also probably be weakened in Hong Kong as its construction and layout was deliberately designed to mess with the flow of energies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T08:21:35-07:00","id":159995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149969-entitlements-for-the-directional-courts?p=157032#post157032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Directional courts, if you're basing them on the idea of feng shui, would also probably be weakened in Hong Kong as its construction and layout was deliberately designed to mess with the flow of energies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds interesting. Would you expand on this comment? What were the goals of this layout complexity?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T05:14:16-07:00","id":165812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149969-entitlements-for-the-directional-courts?p=159995#post159995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That sounds interesting. Would you expand on this comment? What were the goals of this layout complexity?</div> </div> </div> </div> AFAIK? To denegrate traditional Chinese belief in favor of new Communist ideals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T05:35:31-07:00","id":165827,"title":"","content":"Order of the Hallowed Garden would be a good fit. Sounds like there could be a schism. One with traditional feng shui values and that works to upset the energies in favor of other ideals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T03:58:43-07:00","id":171537,"title":"","content":"I'm actually statting up Hong Kong too. A very interesting city for a freehold.<br /> <br /> I'm changing Bodhisattvas of the Broken Cage into South Court (in my version of Hong Kong the seasonal courts are pretty set-in-their-ways and traditional). Twilight Gleaners also fit for me because of a long history of using divination in Chinese power structures. Guild of Gildspinners was already mentioned; depending on the flavor you want you can go Satrapy of Pearls on that one.<br /> <br /> Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue is a great suggestion too, definitely.<br /> <br /> Also, depending on your view of the North Bishopric of Blackbirds might fit them. Good deeds and all that. And Lords of the Unknown Reaches (AFB not sure about the name, the one that deals with supernaturals other than the Fae) can fit in nicely with the East because from the write-up they are also the ones dealing with death/ghosts/etc.<br /> <br /> And my freehold definitely has one Draconic Vizier. Because a freehold in Hong Kong NEEDS a Draconic Vizier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}